  "body": "# OpenTT3D development .46 \u2014 runtime catalogue closure\n\nThis is a development prerelease. The authored runtime ledger now has **2,887\nentries, all at 9/10**; 183 retained non-runtime references remain separately at\n3/10. The reviewed title world reports zero unmodelled reference sprites.\n[Immutable `.42`](https://github.com/cstanislav/opentt3d/releases/tag/opentt3d-dev-20261003.42)\nremains the recommended playable checkpoint until the independent matrix passes.\n\n## Included work\n- Authored 3D disaster body/shadow volumes close the final original runtime\n  sprite family; all fifteen subtypes and all 23 source sprites are bound.\n- Road slopes and road-waypoint signs now use world-space 3D geometry.\n- Locks use the complete map-owned 3D wall family, including independent source\n  face culling.\n- The Toyland factory 144 completed state now has a 3D finished-factory body.\n- The previous orange-cube branding, road-stop asphalt, stepped canal quays,\n  centred bank cupolas, nightly CI repairs, README/screenshots and pinned\n  OpenGFX2 work are retained.\n\n## Verification and limits\nLocal asset/harness/native/presentation tests pass; the packaged macOS-arm64\ncandidate passed Vulkan and OpenGL package controls and an actual title-world save\nwith zero unmodelled-reference report. Natural company-score HQ selection, custom\nriver-source absence/phases, LOD/picking/ship-clearance, sustained 60fps/memory,\nand the full hosted independent platform/input/replay/network matrix remain open.\nDownloads are attached only after the packaging jobs and independent checks pass.\n",
  "databaseId": 438710860,
